				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				751,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Implement per-subsystem tier resolution in TauriChannel IPC routing\n\nIntroduce per-subsystem tier assignment so IPC channels can route to either Mountain (Tauri backend) or Node (Cocoon extension host) independently, rather than being governed by the single global `_TierIPC` variable.\n\nAdd `_ReadTier` to read per-subsystem overrides from `import.meta.env` or `globalThis.__LandTiers`, with defaults that keep most routes on \"Mountain\" but route `tasks` and `auth` to \"Node\" by default. `_ResolveTierForRoute` maps route prefixes (`terminal`, `git`, `language`, `search`, `model`, etc.) to their configured tier. `TauriChannel.Call` and the fallback no-route path both consult the per-subsystem tier instead of — or alongside — the global `_TierIPC`, so e.g. a `tasks:List` call goes to Cocoon even when `TierIPC` is \"Mountain\".\n\nThis is the Output-side counterpart of the matching change in `Wind/Source/Service/TauriMainProcessService.ts` (TIER-SYSTEM Step 4b). The compiled `.js` and source map are regenerated from the updated `.ts`.",
			"SHA": "cac1b663c47e6f535d5449d208dacdd8d941ab08"
		},
